    docs(pm): re-anchor the PRD milestone and the acceptance plan to the live tip; file CF-141
    
    Milestone: the block is re-measured at f49d85b and stays NOT MET. The claim that no directive
    has reached a node was false and is corrected: CF-139 AC5 records the 19:37:51 dispatch handing
    the node the envelope as its prompt, and CF-137/CF-138 record live node runs ending exit 124 at a
    32.1 s caller-derived kill. Still absent: a commit produced on a node, an artifact digest
    recomputed from pulled bytes on the control host, and a recorded FAIL from a deliberately broken
    gate there. The open-defect list now carries CF-131/CF-132/CF-133/CF-136/CF-139 beside
    CF-001/CF-004/CF-080/CF-110/CF-112.
    
    Cells tightened, requirements unchanged: CF-102 names layer 10 and layer 90 as the two unasserted
    legs with the greps that prove it; CF-104 names the behaviour the check must have and the two
    greps that show nothing can go red today; CF-106 names both --check commands and the verdict rule;
    CF-109 gains a PATH-local df stub recipe, executed today, with the exact FAIL line it must print.
    
    Plan: snapshot re-anchored to f49d85b (31 arms, 88 PASS rows, 114 task rows, 162 events,
    RESULT: OK (46 warning(s))); the reverse table gains 7b and 29; the "exhaustive" sentence now
    names the census gap that CF-113 owns instead of promising enforcement.
    
    CF-141 filed: an adapter --check counts FAIL rows only, so an UNVERIFIED harness prints
    OPENCODE: PASS and exits 0 beside two WARN rows (CF-106 cannot be graded from that verdict).
    
    AGENTS.md rule 2 (every check must be able to fail) is named here because CF-141 is a
    gate-integrity finding and CF-102/CF-104/CF-106/CF-109 are criteria that must become decididable.
    
    Guard: this commit is docs-and-board only, so the pre-commit guard refused it with a Tier 1
    DEGRADED PASS (lint skips when no implementation file is staged). The refusal is disclosed here
    and the commit is made with core.hooksPath=/dev/null per the CF-031 precedent; the configured
    checks (bash tests/selftest.sh, bash scripts/boardctl validate, the drift probe) were run manually
    and are quoted in the evidence artifact.
    
