 {"id":"CF-139","title":"P0 - the scheduler dispatches an envelope with no instruction, so every remote task is asked to run a JSON blob","status":"in_progress","priority":"P0","complexity":3,"reasoning":null,"acceptance_criteria":"1. WorkItem carries the lane's rendered directive text and the payload includes it under a non-reserved key, so the node receives an instruction. 2. The rendered directive comes from the lane's configured prompt, not from json.dumps of the envelope; a dry run shows prose. 3. The dispatcher refuses a dispatch whose text is empty or is itself a JSON object, proven by a test. 4. A remote tick produces a harness transcript that shows the directive it was given. 5. Evidence: internal/bus/dispatch.go payload() emits kind/lane/corr_id/scheduler_id/issued_at/board/workdir/reply_to and states 'No task field exists'; the 19:37:51 dispatch fed the node {\"kind\": \"work.dispatch\", ...} as its prompt.","detail":{"fingerprint":"96bdc2bfbb746f20147de275a39738b589ec4a31418963ca88f9b78298523b4e"},"created_at":"2026-11-04T00:43:38Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T00:59:07Z"}
 {"id":"CF-140","title":"P3 — clone_lane.py mints a lane with the source lane's cooldown and pin, and disables a live lane on re-run","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Measured by the code-factory-qa tick code-factory-qa-2026-11-04-00-07-40 at origin/main d586336, in a detached worktree (git worktree add --detach <scratch> origin/main), probe executed from the repo root.\n\nscripts/clone_lane.py is the shipped tool that mints a lane row by cloning a canonical sibling (docstring: the scheduler's lane-onboarding gate refuses every workdir for docs/readme/perf/review families, so cloning a live row is the only way to give a new project the same shape). It reads the source row with SELECT * and copies the WHOLE row (`row = dict(src)`), overriding only name, workdir, namespace_id, parent, enabled=0, repo_url, prompt_mode, the three last_tick_* fields, consecutive_failures, created_at and updated_at. Everything else is inherited verbatim: cooldown_s, cooldown_pin_s, cooldown_pin_by, cooldown_pin_at, the bump_* set, board_rows_seen/board_open_seen and the qa/pm/sync/dogfood zero-output counters.\n\nThat inheritance is not theoretical: 868 of the 876 rows in ~/.hermes/coding-hermes/scheduler.db carry cooldown_pin_s > 0 today (values include 604800 = 7d, 21600 = 6h), so a clone of almost any live lane starts its life pinned. The cloned lane is written enabled=0, so the pin is invisible until an operator enables it — and enabling does not clear cooldown_pin_s, so the new lane's first tick is up to seven days away with no output and no error. That is the same user-visible outcome CF-134 (P1) describes, reached through a different mechanism.\n\nTwo more defects in the same write path, both reproduced by the probe: (1) when the destination name already exists the tool prints \"already exists — configuring it instead of creating\" and then UPDATEs every cloned column, including enabled=0, so re-running it to re-point a live lane silently DISABLES that lane and overwrites its own 900 s cooldown with the source's 604800 s; (2) repo_url is hardcoded to local:~/code-factory and ignores --workdir entirely, so a clone whose workdir is anywhere else is written with a repo_url that contradicts its own workdir — exactly the intra-family disagreement scripts/lane_target.py's CF-091 check exists to reject.\n\nBoundary against existing rows: CF-134 is the pin VALUES freezing the fleet and is fixed by unpinning rows; this is the mint tool's write path, which re-imports pins from any source row, so CF-134 can close and a single clone_*_lane invocation reintroduces one. CF-085 (complete) fixed repo_url INHERITANCE for satellites at mint time; this is a hardcoded path that ignores both the source and --workdir. No row on the board mentions clone_lane.py (census over id/title/reasoning at d586336: 0 hits).","acceptance_criteria":"1. Repro on the current tree: the row's probe prints new-lane with cooldown_s=604800 and cooldown_pin_s=604800 inherited from the 604800 s source lane, and prints live-lane (created enabled=1, cooldown_s=900) as enabled=0, cooldown_s=604800, cooldown_pin_s=604800 after the tool is re-run on the existing name.\n2. After the fix, `scripts/clone_lane.py --from <src> --to <new>` writes cooldown_s=900 (or the explicit --cooldown-s value) and leaves cooldown_pin_s NULL, cooldown_pin_by='' and cooldown_pin_at='' on the new lane regardless of the source row's values; the probe's new-lane line must read cooldown_s=900 and an empty pin.\n3. After the fix, re-running the tool on an EXISTING lane preserves that lane's enabled flag and its own cooldown_s; an overwrite requires --force, and the tool prints the field names it changed. The probe's live-lane line must read enabled=1, cooldown_s=900.\n4. After the fix, repo_url is derived from --workdir (`git -C <workdir> rev-parse --show-toplevel`) or accepted explicitly via --repo-url, so a clone whose workdir is not a ~/code-factory checkout never prints local:/home/kara/code-factory; the probe's two written rows show repo_url matching $d/wd.\n5. The tool refuses to mutate the scheduler DB silently: --dry-run (or the default) prints the row diff and writes nothing, and a missing --prompt file exits non-zero before any write; a test covers both.\n6. Gate at the fix commit: `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints SELFTEST: PASS with rc 0 and `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints RESULT: OK; the probe extracted from the committed board and run from the repo root exits 0 and prints the post-fix table.","detail":{"fingerprint":"fbeaa33bebdd76dcf936cdc19afda00e40148e8e6bd85ce3806a03d81f2ea93c"},"created_at":"2026-11-04T00:48:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T00:48:35Z","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); printf '%s\\n' 'CREATE TABLE projects (name TEXT PRIMARY KEY, repo_url TEXT, workdir TEXT, enabled INTEGER, cooldown_s INTEGER, namespace_id TEXT, parent TEXT, prompt TEXT, prompt_mode TEXT, last_tick_started TEXT, last_tick_completed TEXT, last_tick_status TEXT, consecutive_failures INTEGER, created_at TEXT, updated_at TEXT, cooldown_pin_s INTEGER, cooldown_pin_by TEXT, cooldown_pin_at TEXT, admission_mode TEXT, cooldown_floor_s INTEGER);' \"INSERT INTO projects VALUES('src-lane','local:/x/y','/x/y',1,604800,'ns','','','append','','','',0,'t','t',604800,'fleet-toml-import','2026-11-01T00:00:00Z','',0);\" \"INSERT INTO projects VALUES('live-lane','local:/x/y','/x/y',1,900,'ns','','','append','','','',0,'t','t',NULL,'','','',0);\" | sqlite3 \"$d/s.db\"; sed \"s#^DB = os.path.expanduser.*#DB = '$d/s.db'#\" scripts/clone_lane.py > \"$d/clone.py\"; python3 \"$d/clone.py\" --from src-lane --to new-lane --workdir \"$d/wd\" --namespace ns --parent p >/dev/null; echo \"clone_rc=$?\"; python3 \"$d/clone.py\" --from src-lane --to live-lane --workdir \"$d/wd\" --namespace ns --parent p >/dev/null; echo \"reconfigure_rc=$?\"; sqlite3 -header -column \"$d/s.db\" \"select name,enabled,cooldown_s,cooldown_pin_s,repo_url from projects order by name\"; rm -rf \"$d\""}
+{"id":"CF-141","title":"P4 — an adapter --check verdict counts FAIL rows only, so an UNVERIFIED harness prints PASS beside its own WARN rows (CF-106 cannot be graded from it)","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured at f49d85b with a PATH-local stub opencode that answers --version and advertises no run/exec/serve mode: `bash scripts/harness/install-opencode.sh --check` prints `WARN user_space_binary`, `WARN non_interactive`, then `OPENCODE: PASS` and exits 0 — beside its own banner line `harness: opencode (UNVERIFIED adapter)`. The summary at scripts/harness/install-opencode.sh:37 tests `$FAILED` only (same shape at install-hermes.sh:106 and install-claude-code.sh:43), so a WARN row can never affect the verdict. specs/HARNESS.md:29 says an unmeasured adapter must be marked UNVERIFIED, so `PASS` contradicts the spec status, and the PRD CF-106 cell would read this verdict as harness support. The two adapters also disagree on whether a verdict line exists at all: on this host `install-hermes.sh --check` exits 1 printing `FAIL python — hermes-agent 0.19.0 requires python >=3.11,<3.14; found 3.14.9` and no `HERMES:` line.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Reproduce on the current tree, from the repository root: the row's probe prints two `WARN` rows (`user_space_binary`, `non_interactive`), then `OPENCODE: PASS`, then `rc=0`, for a stub harness whose `--help` advertises no run/exec/serve mode — the adapter's own banner already says `UNVERIFIED adapter`.\n2. Every harness adapter's `--check` ends with one verdict line from a fixed vocabulary, decided by row counts, not by `$FAILED` alone: `PASS` only when every contract row is `PASS`; `UNVERIFIED` when at least one row is `WARN` and none is `FAIL`; `FAIL (n)` when any row is `FAIL`, with exit status nonzero. The chosen exit status for `UNVERIFIED` is stated in `specs/HARNESS.md` (spec first, per `AGENTS.md` rule 1).\n3. Three arms in `tests/selftest.sh`, each asserting the printed verdict by name against a PATH-local stub adapter: (a) a stub with a `WARN` row prints `UNVERIFIED` and never `PASS`; (b) a stub with a `FAIL` row prints `FAIL (n)` and exits nonzero; (c) an all-`PASS` stub prints `PASS` and exits 0. The three arms share one fixture so only the stub's row counts differ.\n4. `scripts/harness/install-hermes.sh` and `scripts/harness/install-claude-code.sh` print that same verdict line for the same three arms — today `install-hermes.sh --check` on a host with an unsupported interpreter exits 1 printing `FAIL python — …` and no verdict line at all, so a caller cannot tell a verdict from a crash.\n5. `specs/HARNESS.md` defines the verdict vocabulary and the UNVERIFIED rule, and the PRD's CF-106 `Verified by` cell cites this row's arms instead of describing them.\n6. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` with the three new arms' `  PASS` rows and no `FAIL` rows of its own, and `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK` at the fixed tip.\n7. The commit carries a `ch:trace` marker naming row CF-141, the three selftest arms and the evidence artifact, and its message states `AGENTS.md` rule 2 (every check must be able to fail).","detail":{"fingerprint":"c98e9969616dcd0cb2d1c3b32f666130a679d19498cd2d58e259d311d1c0d349"},"created_at":"2026-11-04T01:48:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T01:48:00Z","probe":"d=$(mktemp -d); mkdir -p \"$d/bin\"; printf '#!/bin/sh\\nif [ \"$1\" = \"--version\" ]; then echo 9.9.9; else echo \"opencode cli help\"; fi\\n' > \"$d/bin/opencode\"; chmod +x \"$d/bin/opencode\"; PATH=\"$d/bin:$PATH\" HOME=\"$d\" bash scripts/harness/install-opencode.sh --check; echo rc=$?"}
